@name Explainer 11b: double Gauss 50mm f/2
# Explainer #11b: six-element double Gauss, f/2, catalogue glasses (N-LAK9
# crowns, N-SF5 flints), two cemented doublets around the stop. An
# alternative to lenses/double-gauss.lens, whose Abbe numbers are assumed
# (its C-F focus shift is 2.4x the triplet's).
# Role: tuning the two halves separately makes f/2 sharp.
# Design: started from lenses/double-gauss.lens; all curvatures,
# thicknesses and spacings vary (EFL 50 mm, stop gaps >= 2 mm), minimising
# the white-light RMS spot at 0, 0.5, 0.7 and 1.0 of the field, object at
# 2.5 m; vignetting towards the corner up to half the light.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/explainer/11b-double-gauss.toml`.
# RMS spot (F, e, C) at f/2, object at 2.5 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 16.8, 0.5: 14.7, 0.7: 17.8, 1: 19.8 µm. Units: mm.
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
